IN THE COURT OF THE LEARNED CIVIL JUDGE / ADDITIONAL DISTRICT JUDGE, UDAIPUR

Civil Suit No. ______ of 2025

Smt. Kamla Devi                                                          … Plaintiff / Applicant

Versus

Shri Vikram Singh                                                        … Defendant / Non-Applicant

APPLICATION UNDER ORDER 39 RULES 1 AND 2 READ WITH SECTION 151 CPC
FOR TEMPORARY INJUNCTION / STATUS QUO

MOST RESPECTFULLY SHOWETH:

1. That the applicant has filed the accompanying suit for permanent injunction restraining the Defendant from interfering with her possession and easementary rights over a 10-ft wide passage.

2. That the applicant is the owner in possession of House No. 22 and has been using the said passage openly, peacefully and continuously for more than 20 years as of right.

3. That the Defendant has commenced digging foundation and stacking construction material with the clear intention of blocking the passage. Photographs and site inspection will demonstrate the ongoing interference.

4. That a strong prima facie case exists. The balance of convenience is wholly in favour of the applicant. If the temporary injunction is not granted, the applicant will suffer irreparable injury – loss of access, light and air – which cannot be compensated in money.

5. That the applicant has approached this Hon’ble Court with clean hands and without any delay.

PRAYER

It is therefore most respectfully prayed that this Hon’ble Court may be pleased to:

(a) Restrain the Defendant, his agents and any person claiming through him from digging, constructing, stacking material or in any manner obstructing or interfering with the 10-ft wide passage described in Schedule-B of the plaint, and from interfering with the Plaintiff’s possession of the suit property, till the final disposal of the suit;

(b) Direct the parties to maintain status quo with regard to the suit property and the passage; and

(c) Pass any other order as this Hon’ble Court may deem fit and proper.

Place: Udaipur
Date: _______________

